    <section class="py-16 bg-warm">
      <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-5 lg:px-8">
        <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl text-ink mb-6">What if my partner will not come?</h2>
        <p class="text-ink-muted leading-relaxed mb-4">This comes up often, and the process does not stop there. You can start on your own. Working on your own part in the pattern can be enough to change one end of the cycle.</p>
        <p class="text-ink-muted leading-relaxed">We cover this in more detail here: <a href="/en/blog/couples-therapy-famagusta.html" class="text-primary underline hover:no-underline">Couples Therapy in Famagusta: When, Why and How to Start</a></p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="py-16 bg-white">
      <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-5 lg:px-8">
        <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl text-ink mb-6">Do we have to be married?</h2>
        <p class="text-ink-muted leading-relaxed mb-4">No. Marriage is not a precondition. We work with couples who live together, are engaged, are in a long-distance relationship, or are early in a relationship.</p>
        <p class="text-ink-muted leading-relaxed">Couples considering separation also come. In that case the work is not about keeping the relationship going but about being able to think the decision through together, with less damage. Therapy does not promise an outcome; it opens room for a person and a relationship to understand themselves.</p>
      </div>
    </section>
